  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Artic Cards on the Clinic Table",
    "overview": "Talk Lab is a deck of articulation cards laid on a cool grey desk, not a website with a row of tabs. Each goal is a crisp white card wearing a thick coloured top edge; the goal in play lifts out of the deck, and the word card in the game wears that same colour. Everything else stays quiet: one ink-navy for primary actions and the selected section, one legible typeface, flat white surfaces at rest.\n\nThis world (Artic cards) replaced the dealt direction (Playground); the user chose it. It was built from a fresh world, not a catalog seed, so no world: or seededFrom provenance is carried. Density is working-tool density: three sections (Session, Plan, Progress), each meant to fit one screen on an iPad, with clinician controls close but calm so the child's game stays the focus.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
